      <Quiz id="quiz-search" questions={quiz} />
      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li>A search gives back the target's index, or -1 when it is not there.</li>
          <li>Linear search checks one value after another. It works on any order, but may need every value (n checks).</li>
          <li>Binary search checks the middle and throws away half. It needs <b>sorted</b> data and an array, and needs only about 20 checks for 1,000,000 values.</li>
          <li>In Java: <code>while (low &lt;= high)</code>, <code>mid = (low + high) / 2</code>, then <code>low = mid + 1</code> or <code>high = mid - 1</code>.</li>
          <li>Java's <code>Arrays.binarySearch</code> does it for you, on a sorted array.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
